topics.text:
How many numbers with 6 digits we can form using only the characters 1, 2, 3 and 4 (all of them) with the following rules:



- second digit can't be the same as the first;

- third digit can't be the same as the second;

- fourth digit can't be the same as the third;

- fifth digit can't be the same as the fourth;

- sixth digit can't be the same as the fourth;



Attention for the last rule: it is fourth, not fifth.
